# Virtual ride (C3a): `monkeyc -f "monkey.jungle;ride.jungle"`, only through
# `tools/sim.py ride`. It is the demo (`demo.jungle`) with the motorcycle moving: it swaps the
# `demoAfterLoad` that holds the screen (`demo/source/DemoHold.mc`, annotated
# `demo_hold`) for the one in `demo/ride/RideStart.mc`. `bin/ride/RideParams.mc` is
# generated by `sim.py` on every run, from the `.esperado.json`.
base.sourcePath = source;demo/source;demo/ride;bin/ride
base.resourcePath = resources;demo/resources
base.excludeAnnotations = canary;quadratic_parse;nodemo;demo_hold;no_near_alert
